# Print PDF layout lock (approved)

Treat the current generated print PDF and approval sheets as **locked**. Do not redesign the business card or invent spacing from diagrams.

## Source of truth

1. **Generated production PDF** (`src/helpers/printPdf.js` + `src/helpers/cardLayout.js`) owns page geometry and final placement.
2. **Approval images** in `docs/samples/print-pdf/` are the visual lock for client approval:
   - `Colliers-Print-PDF-Approval-Standard.png`
   - `Colliers-Print-PDF-Approval-Maximum.png`
3. Written rules: `docs/samples/print-pdf/LAYOUT-GUIDE.md` and `docs/PRINT-PDF.md`.
4. Fixtures: `src/helpers/approvalSamples.js` (Standard + Maximum). Regenerate with `npm run export:approval-guide`.

## Geometry (do not change without explicit approval)

| Spec | Value |
| --- | --- |
| MediaBox / BleedBox | 270 × 162 pt |
| TrimBox | `[9, 9, 261, 153]` |
| Final trim | 252 × 144 pt |
| Bleed | 9 pt / ⅛ in every side |
| Address | X = 27 · 80 pt wide · bottom Y = 27 · max 5 lines |
| Identity | X = 113.03 · 130 pt wide |

`3_5x2_BusCrd_MASTER.pdf` is **trim-only**. Use it only for typography / composition. MASTER → production is **+9 pt X/Y**. Never strip bleed from the production spec because MASTER has none.

## Hard rules

- Do **not** redraw the card as field blocks, UI wireframes, or spacing rectangles.
- Do **not** invent gaps from bounding-box edges (“8 pt empty band”).
- Website must fit **one line ≤ 130 pt**. Email may use **≤ 132 pt** so real Colliers first.lastname addresses fit; character count alone is not enough.
- Name wraps by whole words, max **2 lines**; layout may fail under 50 characters.
- Optional rows omit when empty. On Standard (no own-row credentials), name/title stay on MASTER Ys (75.49 / 66.99). Unused air between title (or team) and the bottom-locked email is the client-approved short-card gap. Do not pack short cards up from email.
- Own-row / Maximum: if team (or the last identity line) would sit tighter than the Standard team→email gap (`emailGapMin` 15.99 pt), lift the identity block so the last line is at **58.99**. Contacts stay bottom-locked (email 43 / mobile 35 / website 27). Cynthia Oct 2026: extra space above email on the long card.
- Website / last address line share baseline Y = 27. Email and mobile stack up at 8 pt.
- Maximum approval is a **valid stress case**, not an overflow demo.
- Keep Standard / Maximum fixtures and approval PNGs in sync after any intentional layout change.

## Allowed without reopening the lock

- Bug fixes that restore parity with the locked approval sheets
- Klai mirror sync that matches Vue `cardLayout` / `printPdf`
- Docs clarifying the locked rules (no new coordinates)
